From a5be8ad19da8596222f18ed3a5c60dac807c4864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDR in YCbCr 4:2:0 at 10 bits where RGB
 would leave at 8

amdgpu sends HDR at 2160p50 and 2160p60 over TMDS as RGB at 8 bits:
fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode() lowers the depth until
the TMDS clock fits (adjust_colour_depth_from_display_info()), and
turns to YCbCr 4:2:0 only where not even 8 bits fit. It follows now the
rule of drm_dvbridge_hdr.h (linux-9966), as i915 does: where HDR video
(PQ or HLG) over TMDS HDMI was fitted in RGB below 10 bits per
component, the timing is made again in 4:2:0, at the depth the sink
takes in 4:2:0 capped by max bpc, as for a mode the sink takes in 4:2:0
only, and lowered until the TMDS clock fits; it is kept when that is 10
bits or more, and otherwise the RGB timing stays. The gate of the depth
is max bpc as create_validate_stream_for_sink() tries it and the sink's
deep colour in RGB as DRM reads it, as i915 has both in its pipe bpp.
DC validates the stream as any other; a 4:2:0 stream it refused at that
depth is tried again with a lower max bpc, down to 8, where the rule no
longer applies, so no mode is lost. The output colour space is then
BT.2020 YCbCr (get_output_color_space()), and DC encodes and signals it
with the BT.2020 matrix already. A format forced in debugfs is left as
it is, and so is HDMI FRL.

The stream is made again when DVBRIDGE_HDR_YCBCR420 changes, or when
HDR metadata starts or stops having the PQ or HLG transfer function
without the metadata coming or going (that already forces a modeset);
a stream that comes out the same is no modeset (dm_update_crtc_state()).

The HDMI connectors whose encoder sends 4:2:0 get DVBRIDGE_HDR_YCBCR420
("deep" by default; not gated by amdgpu.dvbridge, the rule is no part
of the tunnel), and, beside the HDR10 depth guard, DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT,
written by amdgpu_dm_hdr10_guard_check() for every request of the
guard, with any metadata or none, from the stream of the commit
(encoding and depth), and 0 when the connector has none. A request of
the guard puts the CRTC in the commit for that, without a modeset. The
kernel log of a refusal of the guard says why 4:2:0 was not sent
instead. dvbridge_depth_bpc() is shared with amdgpu_dm.c.

Built with W=1 on the changed files, without warnings; the rule and a
model of its use here are tested on the host (linux-9966).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c   |  10 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_mode.h      |   7 +
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 124 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.h |  14 ++
 .../amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_refused.c    |  70 ++++++++--
 5 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

